<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34132" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pătrĭarcha</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pătrĭarches</span></b> ,
			ae, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατριάρχης</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the father</i> or <i>chief of a
			tribe</i>, <i>a patriarch.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">secundum patriarchas et ceteros majores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Idol. 17</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Cor. Mil. 9</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Prud. Psych. 534</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1 Par.
				8, 28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Act. 7, 8</span></i>.—<i>Gen. plur.</i> patriarchūm,
					<i><span class="en">Paul. Nol. Carm. 24,
			209</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a chief
			bishop</i>, <i>a patriarch</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Vop. Firm. Saturn. 8,
			4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">philosophi, patriarchae ut ita dixerim,
					haereticorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
